'''Willi Mapu''' ({{Literal translation|land of the south}}), alternatively spelled '''Willimapu''', is a predominately {{W|Mapuche|Wallche}} [[Indigenous nations in Balisca|indigenous territory]] in western [[Cerdanya]], and one of the [[Regions of Balisca|13 regions of the community]]. It borders [[Küyenmapu]] to the northwest, [[Camaca]] to the southeast, [[Pigüe]] to the north, and the [[Salsipuedes Sea]] to the south.

It has an area of {{convert|109548.43|km2|mi2|abbr=on}} making it the # largest region of Balisca, and it is the second most-populous indigenous territory in Balisca, with an estimated population of 823,766 as of 1 April 2026. The administrative center and the most populous settlement within is [[Peñalolén]] ("fraternal meeting place"). 

